    "abstract": "International audience",
    "field": "Aerosol radiative forcing",
    "problem": "Assessing the climatic effect of mineral dust is highly uncertain because its radiative forcing is very sensitive to the large, poorly constrained variability in its physical properties (refractive index, size distribution), vertical profile, and underlying surface conditions, leading to large errors in climate models.",
    "method": "This paper investigates the validity of approximations in climate models by using a single-column radiation model to assess the sensitivity of mineral dust's radiative forcing to parameters such as aerosol refractive index, size distribution, vertical profile, and surface properties for representative desert and oceanic cases.",
    "task": "This paper investigates uncertainties in calculating the direct radiative forcing of mineral dust by performing a sensitivity study on key parameters, such as aerosol refractive index and size distribution, using a single-column radiation model for desert and oceanic cases.",
